":"https://api.github.com/users/ctuyu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ctuyu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ctuyu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ctuyu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ctuyu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ctuyu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ctuyu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-15T08:57:26Z","updated_at":"2026-09-15T08:57:26Z","body":"> > Completed jobs left after the final post_step() were freed without destroying their callbacks.\r\n> \r\n> This would imply that there were jobs that didn't have `JPH::JobSystem::FreeJob` called for them at the end of `JPH::PhysicsSystem::Update`, which I don't believe should even be possible in the first place. The test you provided is not really a supported use-case either.\r\n> \r\n> What symptoms were you seeing as a result of this issue exactly?\r\n\r\nThanks for the reply.The observed symptom is a Jolt task-pool assertion during shutdown in a development build, not a crash. It occurs when shared workers are busy: physics work finishes, but queued worker callbacks release their job references after the final post_step(), leaving those jobs unreclaimed. Adding the destructor drain removes the assertion.  ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5677492129/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5678026884","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123487#issuecomment-5678026884","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123487","id":5678026884,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUm_QhA",